# Harness rules

The template owns this file (agent-harness {{ harness_ref }}) and `copier update` replaces it: never edit it here,
put project facts in CLAUDE.md. Everything else is derived: `uv run dev --help` lists commands,
`docs/generated/agent-surface.md` lists agents, skills, hooks, plugins and MCP servers, `docs/research/INDEX.md` lists
what is already researched, [decisions.md](../docs/generated/decisions.md) the durable rules and their reasons.

## Every session
- The board is GitHub issues: `uv run dev board next`, `board brief <n>`, `board claim <n> --agent <name>`.
  Work without an issue does not exist. Each issue has a measurable DONE WHEN. A small fix found on the way
  belongs to the current issue: the fix-now rule (multi-agent.md §3).
- The main session is the lead: the `harness-ops:lead` skill. Workers are `harness-ops:` subagents, one issue each,
  in their own worktree.
- Multi-agent and multi-machine protocol: [multi-agent.md](../docs/specs/multi-agent.md).

## Rules
- Branch `<issue>-<slug>` in a worktree. Only `uv run dev integrate <pr>` merges.
- Run `uv run dev test --affected` while iterating. `uv run dev check` gates the committed HEAD: run it when you
  believe you are done, and again after any fix. Never weaken a check, test or budget to pass. Ask the owner instead.
- **Research before implementing.** Any design or algorithm choice needs a cited note in `docs/research/`.
  Check INDEX.md first and extend an existing note rather than writing a parallel one. Use the research skill.
- Label claims **VERIFIED** (measured here), **SOURCED** (cited and fetched), **BELIEVED** or **ASSUMED**.
- Never read `.env`.
- Re-check a root cause with data before writing it down. First explanations are often wrong.
- Link to a fact where it lives; never copy counts, field lists or commands into prose.
- Unclear requirement: add it to `docs/questions/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md` with your default, then proceed on that default.
- Before editing CLAUDE.md, `.claude/`, `.devkit/`, `[tool.devkit]` or CI, load the `harness-ops:harness` skill.
  Generic changes go to agent-harness itself, then `copier update` here.
